 "transcript": {
  "answer": "The RBA cash rate target is **4.35%**, where it has sat since about June 2026. The latest monthly average, for September 2026, was **4.36%**.\n\nIt has risen from a low of 3.60% over September 2025 to January 2026. The rate then went up in steps: to 3.83% in February, 3.96% in March, 4.10% in April, 4.31% in May, and 4.35% in June. The data stops at September 2026, so I can't see any decision after that. I can also pull the lending rates (variable, fixed, business) if you want to see how the cash rate is flowing through to borrowers.",
